# libndp -- IPv6 Neighbor Discovery, and the one hard external dependency of
# NetworkManager that nothing else in this tree provides.
#
# NM's meson.build line 266 is
#     libndp_dep = dependency('libndp')
# with no `required: false` and no option guarding it, so NetworkManager does not
# configure at all without this. Unlike jansson (optional, packaged for what it
# enables) this one is not a decision.
#
# What it does: IPv6 stateless autoconfiguration. NM uses it to send router
# solicitations and read router advertisements, which is how an IPv6 address and
# default route appear on a network with no DHCPv6 server -- the common case.
# There is no fallback path inside NM; without libndp there is no NM.
#
# BLFS 12.4, pinned here rather than in versions.env -- versions.env is
# regenerated wholesale from the LFS book by tools/pin-versions.sh.
SRC_URL=http://libndp.org/files/libndp-1.9.tar.gz
SRC_SHA256=a8ab214e01dc3a9b615276905395637f391298c84d77651f0cbf0b1082dd2dd4
SRC_DIR=libndp-1.9

# --sysconfdir=/etc and --localstatedir=/var are BLFS's, and they are passed for
# hygiene rather than because this package uses either: libndp installs no
# configuration and no state. They are here so that the default /usr/etc and
# /usr/var cannot appear in a config.h or a generated path if a later version
# starts using them. --disable-static for the usual reason.
#
# NOT PASSED: nothing else. libndp's configure has no dependency probes to name
# -- it is glibc, a library and one tool.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--sysconfdir=/etc --localstatedir=/var --disable-static"
